    <article class="legal-body">
      <header class="legal-head">
        <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
        <p class="legal-meta">Version <%= versao %> · Updated on <%= atualizadoEm %></p>
        <p class="legal-lead">
          By creating an account or booking an experience on AquaTrip, you
          agree to the rules below. Please read the sections on payment and
          cancellation carefully.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section id="objeto">
        <h2>1. What AquaTrip is</h2>
        <p>
          AquaTrip is a platform that brings together water experiences —
          beaches, aquariums, diving, kayaking, fishing, and expeditions —
          and lets you find, book, and pay for them in one place.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>We connect you and process the booking. The party that
          carries out the experience is the partner responsible for
          it.</strong> This distinction matters and comes up again in
          section 6.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="conta">
        <h2>2. Your account</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>You must be 18 years of age or older.</li>
          <li>The information you provide must be true and up to date.</li>
          <li>Your password is personal. You are responsible for whatever is done with your credentials.</li>
          <li>If you suspect unauthorized access, change your password immediately — this ends all open sessions.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="reserva">
        <h2>3. How booking works</h2>
        <ol class="legal-steps">
          <li>You choose the experience, the date, and the number of people.</li>
          <li>The spot is <strong>held temporarily for 15 minutes</strong> for you to complete payment.</li>
          <li>The booking is only <strong>confirmed after the payment is approved</strong> by the provider.</li>
          <li>If payment is not completed within that time, the spot is automatically released to other people.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="legal-note">
          A pending booking does not guarantee the spot beyond the period above. The price and terms are those shown at the time of booking.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="pagamento">
        <h2>4. Payment</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>We accept PIX and credit or debit cards, as available at checkout.</li>
          <li>The amount charged is the one shown on the payment screen, calculated by the server — never an amount sent by your browser.</li>
          <li>Card data is processed directly by the payment provider. AquaTrip does not receive or store your card number or security code.</li>
          <li>Each booking allows only one active charge. Duplicate attempts do not result in a duplicate charge.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="cancelamento">
        <h2>5. Cancellation and refunds</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Pending booking:</strong> can be cancelled at any time, at no charge.</li>
          <li><strong>Confirmed booking:</strong> cancellation triggers a refund request to the payment provider.</li>
          <li>The time it takes for the refund to reach you follows the rules of the payment method and the financial institution — AquaTrip does not control that timeline.</li>
          <li>Partner-specific rules (minimum notice, weather conditions) are shown on the experience page and take precedence when more specific.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="legal-note">
          If the experience is cancelled by the partner, you are entitled to a full refund.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="papel">
        <h2>6. Our role and your limits</h2>
        <p>
          AquaTrip is responsible for the platform's operation: search,
          booking, payment processing, receipts, and support related to
          those processes.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Carrying out the experience</strong> — safety, equipment,
          staff, punctuality, on-site conditions — is the responsibility of
          the partner who runs it. Issues with the service itself should be
          addressed with the partner; we assist with intermediation and,
          when applicable, with refunds.
        </p>
        <p>
          Water activities involve risk. Follow the partner's safety
          instructions and disclose any relevant health restrictions before
          the activity.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="conduta">
        <h2>7. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You may not:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Create fake accounts or impersonate another person</li>
          <li>Attempt to access other users' data or areas</li>
          <li>Circumvent technical limits, test vulnerabilities without authorization, or automate bulk bookings</li>
          <li>Post illegal, offensive content, or content that violates the rights of others</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="conteudo">
        <h2>8. Content and ownership</h2>
        <p>
          The brand, design, and code of the platform belong to AquaTrip.
          Text and images for experiences belong to the respective partners
          or rights holders.
        </p>
        <p>
          By submitting a review or photo, you authorize its display on the
          platform while retaining ownership of it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="suspensao">
        <h2>9. Account suspension</h2>
        <p>
          We may suspend or terminate accounts that violate these terms,
          with prior notice whenever possible. Bookings already confirmed
          and paid for are preserved or refunded.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="alteracoes">
        <h2>10. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          These terms carry a version number. Significant changes are
          communicated, and continued use after an update means you accept
          the new version.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="lei">
        <h2>11. Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          Brazilian law applies, in particular the CDC (Código de Defesa do
          Consumidor, Brazil's Consumer Protection Code), the Marco Civil da
          Internet (Brazil's Internet Civil Rights Framework), and the LGPD
          (Lei Geral de Proteção de Dados, Brazil's data protection law).
          Data handling is described in the
          <a href="/politica-de-privacidade">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <aside class="legal-disclaimer">
        <strong>Note about this document</strong>
        <p>
          This text reflects how the platform actually works (the 15-minute
          hold, webhook confirmation, refunds, no card storage). Even so, it
          <strong>does not replace legal review</strong>. Before operating
          commercially, a lawyer should add the company's legal name, tax ID
          (CNPJ), address, jurisdiction, and the specific clauses of your
          contract with partners.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </article>
